  "question": {
    "text": "The length of a magnet is large compared to its width and breadth. The time period of its oscillation in a vibration magnetometer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The magnent is cut into three equal parts of length <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mi>L</mi> <mn>3</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> each,and three parts are then placed on each other with their like poles together. The time period of this combination will be",
    "image": null
  },
